  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The best result so far is RNA-only scvi_n200/multiprofile/avgpool (config_005, acc=0.650). The only multimodal test (config_030: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat) scored 0.632, slightly *below* the RNA-only baseline, suggesting resnet50 image features add noise rather than signal. The critical remaining question is whether a substantially stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can make multimodal fusion actually surpass the RNA-only ceiling. config_036 isolates exactly this: it keeps the proven-best RNA pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and concat fusion, and swaps only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l. If ViT-L lifts accuracy above 0.650, the final experiment can explore weighted fusion or transformer aggregation on top; if not, we confirm RNA-only is the best strategy and can spend the last budget on a fine-grained RNA-only variant. This single-variable change is the highest-information experiment available given 2 slots remain."
}

